; Styles: one named decision about how a stretch of dungeon looks, is shaped and
; what lives there (docs/tool-refinement-plan.md Phase 5, Game/Style.h).
;
; Fields:
;   display          the style's name, as the palette lists it.
;   room / corridor  themes.cat ids: the look of a room and of a passage.
;   knobs            the generator's settings line (as genpresets.cat stores it).
;   corridor_width   squares: 1 for a dirt tunnel, 2 for a grand hall.
;   tags             what content fits it.
;   monsters         `<id> [weight]`, comma-separated; an absent weight is 1. A
;                    monster's power is its own (monsters.cat), never written here.
;
; The shared library (assets/library) holds more; the palette's Styles section
; adds one to this world with the themes and surfaces it needs.

[small_crypt]
display = Small Crypt
room = crypt_chamber
corridor = crypt_passage
knobs = width:28 height:28 roommin:3 roommax:5 path:5 branches:2 branchmin:1 branchmax:2 loops:0 winding:0.2 irregular:0.2 deadends:2 locks:1 difficulty:0.3 density:0.5 ramp:0.4 boss:0 reward:0.5
corridor_width = 1
tags = undead crypt stone
monsters = skeleton 3, skel_archer, skel_coward, mummy
